export anchor HandheldGameLCDStyle:
    number: 162
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Handheld game LCD
    idea: A grey handheld game console held sideways, whose four shade pea green screen draws the dashboard as a role playing game, with a menu window, a stats sheet, a dialog box greeting, projects as a party with health bars and the chart built from one block per task.
    base: light
    palette:
        shade0: #d0e09a, screen paper and text on dark bars
        shade1: #a8c060, selection, highlighted party rows and the focus fill
        shade2: #4f7a32, inner window lines and last week blocks, never text
        shade3: #173d17, all screen text, borders, bars and this week blocks
        shell: #cfcdc6, device plastic, with highlight #e4e2dc and edge #9c9a93
        frame: #5d6070, the screen surround
        keys: #3b3d4a, the D-pad and the round A and B buttons
        print: #2f3140, labels printed on the shell
        room: #efeee9, the page behind the device
    type:
        The screen uses Lucida Console, DejaVu Sans Mono, Monaco, Courier
        New, monospace in bold caps at 0.04em with smoothing off, 18px
        dialog, 14px project names, 13px body, 11 to 12px details and 16px
        stat values. Shell printing uses Futura, Century Gothic, Trebuchet
        MS, Arial, sans-serif, italic 900 for the Brightwork name and bold
        10 to 13px tracked caps for button labels.
    layout:
        A wide grey shell with a big rounded swoop at the bottom left
        holds a D-pad with Select and Start pills on the left, the screen
        in the middle and tilted round B and A buttons over a speaker
        grille on the right. The dark frame above the screen carries a
        striped label line and a red battery dot, and Brightwork pocket is
        printed under it. On the screen a dark top bar holds Find with a
        field, an A badge New project button and a MSG count. Below, three
        pixel windows across. The left has a MENU window with a triangle
        cursor on Home and Player Mara Okafor, then a STATS window with
        dotted leaders to the four values, overdue inverted. The middle
        has a dialog box with the greeting, the date and an hourglass
        overdue line, with a blinking style down arrow, then a PARTY
        window of six bordered member cards with name, team and due date,
        a status sprite and word, and a health bar with tasks and percent,
        the at risk and behind members highlighted. The right has a LOG
        window with triangle bullets and a TASKS CLEARED window where each
        day is a stack of blocks, one block per task. Below 1120px the
        right windows drop under, and below 860px the screen goes to the
        top with the controls in a row underneath.
    spacing: Pixel steps of 2, 4, 6 and 10px on the screen. Windows sit 10px apart.
    density: Busy like a game menu. Three windows across, collapsing to one column.
    corners: Windows 4px. The shell is 36px with a 90px bottom left swoop. The frame has a 40px bottom right curve.
    borders: Each window has a 3px shade3 line, a 2px paper gap and a 2px shade2 inner line. Member cards have a 2px shade3 line.
    shadows: None on screen. The shell has moulded highlights and keys stand on a 4px solid under edge.
    icons:
        Eight by eight pixel sprites. A heart means On track, a warning
        triangle means At risk, a crossed box means Behind, an hourglass
        marks overdue, and a solid triangle cursor marks the current item.
    focus: A 3px shade3 outline offset 2px with a shade1 fill.
    tone: Game speak in caps, such as Player, Party, Stats, Log and Tasks cleared.
